full_message:
BUG#33615493: Assert failure `local_member_info->get_recovery_status() == MEMBER_OFFLINE`

In BUG#33380840 we added a assert to validate that rejoining members
would be the only ones that do enter a group with a ERROR state,
more precisely:
```
gcs_module->notify_of_view_change_end();
...
    if (autorejoin_module->is_autorejoin_ongoing()) {
      assert(local_member_info->get_recovery_status() ==
             Group_member_info::MEMBER_ERROR);
    } else {
      assert(local_member_info->get_recovery_status() ==
             Group_member_info::MEMBER_OFFLINE);
    }
```
Though these asserts were added too late on the view change handler.
In order to allow their correct evaluation, that is, while the join
or automatic rejoin is ongoing, they must be executed before signal
that the view change handling is complete.
Thence these asserts must be placed before the line
`gcs_module->notify_of_view_change_end();`.

RB: 27442
